>> title: Muhammara
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: walnuts, red pepper, syrian, dip, food processor
>> counters: Shawarma Counter
>> aka: mouhamara, mhammara, mouhammara, red pepper walnut dip
>> servings: 8
>> time: 25 min
>> step.1: toast 5 min
>> step.2: pulse to a coarse meal
>> step.3: pulse to a rough paste
>> step.4: blend in
>> step.5: stream in

Toast @walnuts{1%cup}(100 g) in a #dry skillet{} for ~{5%min}, until they smell nutty.

Pulse @&(~1)toasted walnuts{} with @breadcrumbs{1/3%cup}(30 g; coarse, dry) to a coarse meal in a #food processor{}.

Pulse @roasted red peppers{12%oz}(340 g; peeled and seeded) and @garlic{2%cloves} into @&(~1)walnut meal{} to a rough paste.

Blend @pomegranate molasses{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @lemon juice{1%Tbs}, @Aleppo pepper{1%tsp}, @ground cumin{1/2%tsp}, and @kosher salt{3/4%tsp} into @&(~1)paste{}.

Stream @extra-virgin olive oil{1/3%cup}(80 mL) into @&(~1)muhammara{} with the machine running.
